{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"dame van winkle\" (+ henpecked nagging shrew) (+ lazy idleness indolence) (+ analysis study guide))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_1002636624#5_2221266766","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3629","rank":5,"snippet":"Local History and Mythical Narrative Self Identity Overlapping of Time Rip as an Anti-American Negative evasiveness of Rip’s Wife Rip as Negation of Traditional American Hero \" , \"segment\": \"Rip is settled in that village. Rip Van Winkle is a friendly and tranquil fellow. He is the direct successor of the brave soldiers of Dutch genealogy, famous for his generosity and gentleness. He has only a flaw in him that he is unable to earn profits from any work. In fact, he can help others all day long without getting <cover>lazy at work. He is just unable to work at home. His other remarkable trait is that he is a submissive henpecked husband for his wife; Dame Van Winkle. She even rebukes him, follows him down to the village at which he only listens to her patiently. He is loved by all the villagers who side with him against disputes with his wife.\" , \"start_char\": 2904.000000 , \"title\": \"Rip Van Winkle Summary and Analysis</cover>\" , \"url\": \"https://litpriest.com/short-stories/rip-van-winkle-summary/\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_1089796809#0_2157680530","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_1089796809#1_2157682266","rank":2,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_1089792441#0_2157669214","rank":3,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_1089792441#1_2157671259","rank":4,"relevance":3}]}}
