{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_278218781#5_564836667","relevance":3,"reason":"The Owl Eyes passage directly supports why Dame Van Winkle is portrayed negatively: Rip fears her because she represents leaving the freedom of the forest and returning to work, domestic demands, and village commercialism; it also notes her demands may not have been unreasonable.","learned":"A strong critical explanation is that Dame Van Winkle looks oppressive because Rip experiences ordinary work and household responsibility as tyranny, even though her demands may be reasonable."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3637","reason":"This query produced direct critical evidence about Dame Van Winkle as an oppressive antagonist tied to Rip's escape and freedom, so continuing may find more unjudged passages in the same explanatory vein."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3637"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_1345711009#1_2878394968","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3637","rank":2,"snippet":"circumstance might be owing that meekness of spirit which gained him such universal popularity; for those men are most apt to be obsequious and conciliating abroad, who are under the disciplines of shrews at home. Their tempers, doubtless, are rendered pliant and malleable in the fiery furnace of domestic tribulation; and a curtain lecture is worth all the sermons in the world for teaching virtues of patience and long-suffering.\" In other words, <cover>Dame Van Winkle was the oppressive hand that laid the foundation for Rip Van Winkle to experience the pleasures of life once out of the house, as did the people of the colonies once they escaped the rule of the crown. Rip Van Winkle knew how to make the most out of his freedom </cover>and this aura about him led other people to follow Show More Comparing Washington Irving's Rip Van Winkle and America's War of Independence 1420 Words | 6 Pages Parallels in Washington Irving's Rip Van Winkle and America's War of Independence    The story of Rip Van Winkle is well known throughout American culture.\" , \"start_char\": 780.000000 , \"title\": \"Rip'"}}
