{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_877027687#0_1483969041","relevance":3,"reason":"The GradeSaver analysis directly supports why Dame Van Winkle is portrayed negatively: Rip is framed as kind and loved while unable to help his own household, and she is shown as the henpecking wife who publicly berates him, with villagers siding against her.","learned":"GradeSaver emphasizes the biased social framing: Rip’s household irresponsibility provokes Dame Van Winkle, but the village and narrative sympathy side with Rip, making her look like the negative shrewish obstacle."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3638","reason":"The established study-guide query is still yielding useful GradeSaver/LitCharts-style evidence, so continue to seek more direct passages from reputable study-guide sources."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3638"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_877027687#9_1483984279","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3638","rank":6,"snippet":"Bummel is now in Congress. Rip Van Winkle becomes still more distressed and confused when he asks if they know Rip Van Winkle and the townspeople point out a different <cover>lazy-looking man. He begins to think he is crazy. A familiar woman approaches, and he finds out enough to decide that she is his daughter. She explains that her father went out with his gun one day twenty years ago and was never heard from since. Rip Van Winkle tells everyone that for him it has only been one night, which makes them think he is crazy, too. The one piece of good news is that Dame Van Winkle recently passed away. Peter Vanderdonk, the town’s oldest inhabitant, vouches for Rip Van Winkle and says that he has heard tales passed down about the ghosts of Hendrick Hudson and his men appearing once every twenty years;\" , \"start_char\": 5862.000000 , \"title\": \"Rip Van Winkle and Other Stories “Rip Van Winkle” Summary and Analysis | GradeSaver</cover>\" , \"url\": \"http://www.gradesaver.com/rip-van-winkle/study-guide/summary-rip-van-winkle\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_1089800704#0_2157690714","rank":5,"relevance":2}]}}
